<task id="022" project="smart-todo-r5">
  <metadata>
    <title>Completed status — kanban render support + Show-Completed toggle (FR-07 / F-2)</title>
    <phase>3: Top bar + filter + visuals</phase>
    <gate>003 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .ts query-building + kanban bucketing (queryHelpers.ts, useKanbanColumns.ts) — FULL per CLAUDE.md §8 ("modifying .cs/.ts/.tsx" trigger).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Contained query/bucketing change reusing an already-existing visual treatment (KanbanCard isCompleted) — not architectural — sonnet default per CLAUDE.md §8.5.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>Q</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>003</deps>
    <tags>react, typescript, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Surface Dataverse `sprk_todo.statuscode` = Completed (value 2) as a valid, renderable kanban state, hidden by default, exposed via the "Completed" checkbox inside task 021's filter pane Status category. Today `buildTodoItemsQuery` in src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/services/queryHelpers.ts hard-excludes Completed (`statuscode eq 1 or statuscode eq 659490001` only) and `useKanbanColumns.ts` never sees a Completed item, so no rendering path has been exercised. Make Completed items flow through the existing score-based bucketing (Today/Tomorrow/Future — there is no 4th "Completed" column) and render with the ALREADY-EXISTING `isCompleted` visual treatment in KanbanCard.tsx (statuscode===2 → cardCompleted/titleCompleted classes) without layout breakage.</prompt>

  <role>Spaarke platform developer. Expert in the SmartTodo Kanban bucketing pipeline (useKanbanColumns) and OData query composition. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>When the Status filter's Completed checkbox (task 021) is checked, Completed to-dos are fetched, bucketed into their normal score-based column, and rendered with the existing completed-item styling — with no new kanban column, no drag-drop/selection regression, and no visual breakage. When unchecked (the default), Completed items are excluded exactly as they are today.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-07 (F-2): "surface statuscode 'Completed' as a valid kanban/filter state, hidden by default, with a Show Completed toggle in the filter pane." Task 021 (FR-06) owns the Status-category checkbox UI and the base query-parameterization plumbing (buildTodoItemsQuery gains a statuscode-inclusion parameter). This task's scope is the KANBAN RENDER-side guarantee — verifying/hardening useKanbanColumns.ts and KanbanCard.tsx handle Completed items correctly once the query layer starts returning them — plus regression coverage for the default-hidden behavior. KanbanCard.tsx already derives `isCompleted = todo.statuscode === 2 || todo.statecode === 1` (line ~188) and applies `cardCompleted`/`titleCompleted` styling — this task verifies that treatment is sufficient and extends it only if gaps are found (e.g., completed items sorting oddly, drag-drop mis-firing on a completed card, or the "Dismissed" collapsible section colliding with newly-visible Completed items).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/services/queryHelpers.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/hooks/useKanbanColumns.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/components/KanbanCard/KanbanCard.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/hooks/useTodoItems.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/components/DismissedSection.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Phase 1 hoist gate — useKanbanColumns.ts lives in the shared package this task modifies; hoist must be closed first per plan.md sequencing.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-07: Completed items are excluded by default; only visible when the Status filter's Completed checkbox is on.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT add a 4th "Completed" kanban column — Completed items render inside their existing score-based Today/Tomorrow/Future bucket per the design's "kanban renders Completed without layout breakage" acceptance wording.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT change the composite To Do Score formula/weights (todoScoring.ts) — out of scope, locked per spec MUST rule.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Any new/changed styling uses Fluent v9 semantic tokens only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>kanban-bucketing-and-status-lifecycle</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/spaarke-todo-architecture.md</file>
      <file>projects/smart-todo-r5/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/smart-todo-r5/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Read queryHelpers.ts (statuscode constants at ~line 474-475: 1=Open, 659490001=In Progress, 2=Completed, 659490002=Dismissed; buildTodoItemsQuery at ~line 562), useKanbanColumns.ts bucketing logic, KanbanCard.tsx isCompleted derivation (~line 188) and its styling application, and DismissedSection.tsx to understand how the separate Dismissed (659490002) lane already works as a precedent for "a non-Open/In-Progress state that still renders."</step>
    <step order="1">Confirm (do not re-implement, coordinate with task 021 if it has already landed the parameter) that buildTodoItemsQuery can be called with a statuscode-inclusion set that adds `or statuscode eq 2` when Completed is requested.</step>
    <step order="2">Trace a Completed item through useKanbanColumns.ts's `resolveColumn`/bucketing: verify a statuscode=2 item still gets a valid Today/Tomorrow/Future bucket based on its score/due-date exactly like an Open item (no special-case exclusion exists today since Completed items never previously reached this function — confirm by reading, not by assumption).</step>
    <step order="3">Verify KanbanCard.tsx's existing isCompleted treatment (cardCompleted/titleCompleted classes) renders correctly for a Completed item mixed into a column of non-completed items — no layout shift, no drag-drop interaction bugs (a completed item should probably remain draggable/interactive like any other card unless product intent says otherwise; if ambiguous, keep it interactive and note the decision).</step>
    <step order="4">Add/extend unit tests: default fetch excludes Completed; with Completed included, an item bucketed correctly by score/due-date and rendered with the completed visual treatment; toggling the filter off removes previously-visible Completed items from the next fetch.</step>
    <step order="5">Manually verify no regression in the existing Dismissed-section rendering (statuscode 659490002) — that lane is untouched by this task.</step>
    <step order="6">Grep changed files for hex/rgb literals — zero matches.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: mark 022 ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="8">Document the final Completed-rendering decision (interactive vs read-only, any bucketing edge case found) in projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If task 021's Status-category query parameter shape differs from what this task expects (e.g., a different function signature or a different statuscode encoding), coordinate directly with the parallel work rather than diverging — the two tasks share the same predicate-building surface (see parallel-reason). If irreconcilable without a design decision, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Completed items render without layout breakage">
      <steps>
        <step>Seed or mock a mix of Open, In Progress, and Completed to-dos across different score ranges</step>
        <step>Toggle the Status filter's Completed checkbox on</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Completed items appear in their score-appropriate column with the existing dimmed/strikethrough treatment; no column overflow, no broken drag-drop for adjacent cards</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Default-hidden regression">
      <steps>
        <step>Load the Code Page fresh with the Completed checkbox unchecked (default)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>No Completed items appear anywhere in the kanban, identical to pre-R5 behavior</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render a Completed card in webLightTheme, then webDarkTheme</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Completed styling (dimmed text, strikethrough) adapts via semantic tokens; zero hex/rgb literals</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run vitest in the shared lib + src/solutions/SmartTodo</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">grep for hex/rgb literals</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/services/queryHelpers.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/hooks/useKanbanColumns.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/__tests__/useKanbanColumns.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Completed filter checkbox is unchecked (default), then no statuscode=2 items appear in the fetched set or the kanban — identical to current behavior.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Completed filter checkbox is checked, then statuscode=2 items are fetched and bucketed into their normal score-based column (Today/Tomorrow/Future) — no 4th column is introduced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Completed item renders in a column with non-completed items, then the column layout does not break (no overflow, no card-height regression) and the existing isCompleted visual treatment (dimmed/strikethrough) applies.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the pre-existing Dismissed-section rendering (statuscode 659490002) is unaffected by this change.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass; zero hex/rgb literals via grep; build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec refs: FR-07 (F-2). statuscode constants: 1=Open, 659490001=In Progress, 2=Completed, 659490002=Dismissed. Coordinate the Status/Completed query-parameter shape directly with whoever executes task 021 — parallel-unsafe for exactly this reason.

  COMPLETION (2026-08-16): buildTodoItemsQuery(contactId, regardingFilter, includeCompleted=false) — new optional 3rd param, backward-compatible (existing DataverseService.getActiveTodos call site untouched, still defaults to Completed-hidden). useKanbanColumns.ts required NO behavioral change — verified by reading that bucketTodoItems/resolveColumn/assignColumnByDate bucket purely on due-date + pin state with zero statuscode/statecode reference, so Completed items already flow into their normal Today/Tomorrow/Future bucket with no 4th column; added a documentation block recording this verification + the "keep Completed cards fully interactive" decision. New test file useKanbanColumns.test.ts (Jest-less pure-function pattern matching SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx) covers default-hidden regression, Completed bucketing (overdue/future/undated), pinned-Completed override, and Dismissed-shape non-regression — 4/4 assertions verified executable via a throwaway CommonJS transpile+run (not just type-checked). tsc --noEmit clean in both packages (zero new errors; pre-existing baseline errors in SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx and solutions/SmartTodo unrelated to this task's files). Zero hex/rgb literals. Cross-task dependency surfaced (not reached into): task 021 owns the Status-filter Completed checkbox UI + threading includeCompleted through DataverseService/SmartToDo.tsx. Full detail: projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/task-022-completed-toggle.md.</notes>

